    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0302" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg186"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.34537/126.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gonzales to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 7, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to the treaty signed December 27, 1912, for the enlargement of the
                    Guantanamo Naval Station,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d201-f1"/> I hear through the
                    Secretary of State that the Senate is now ready to ratify the treaty. Owing,
                    however, to the expiration of the six months limit it will be necessary to draw
                    up and sign a new treaty. Identical treaty, with change of Article V eliminating
                    time limit, would be acceptable here. Will the Department advise me as to what
                    action it wishes taken in this matter?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
